    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds an audit log line emitted to the dedicated `AUDIT` logger whenever an owner is successfully created.\n\n**What I did:**\n\n1. **Created `OwnerAuditLogger`** (`rest/controller/OwnerAuditLogger.java`) \u2014 a small `@Component` with a single responsibility: emit one `AUDIT`-logger line for a created owner, carrying the owner `id`, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`. This mirrors the existing helper-component style in that package (`EmailNormalizer`, `DailyRegistrationLimitValidator`, etc.) and keeps logging concerns out of the controller.\n\n2. **Wired it into `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 injected via the constructor and invoked with `ownerAuditLogger.logCreated(owner)` immediately after `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`, the point at which `id`, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate` are all populated.\n\n**Why here:** `addOwner` is the sole handler for `POST /api/owners`, and `saveOwner` is where the customer code, namesake count, and generated id get finalized \u2014 so logging just after the save guarantees all three audited fields are present. Emission happens only on the success path (after all validators pass and the save completes).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreLogsAuditOnCreate` and the full build pass. The emitted line looks like:\n\n```\nINFO  AUDIT - Owner created: id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-21\n```",
